# Real-world example: collect and triage a software bug consistently.

CONTEXT
    Produce a concise Markdown bug report with these sections in this order:
    Title, Severity, Environment, Steps to reproduce, Expected behavior,
    Actual behavior. Use only the supplied information and do not invent facts.
AS report_format

PRINT "Bug intake started. I will collect the required details in order."

ASK "Enter a short bug title." AS title
IF @title == ""
    RETURN "Bug intake stopped: a title is required."

ASK "Where does the bug happen? Type exactly: production, staging, or local" AS environment
IF @environment is anything other than production, staging, or local
    RETURN "Bug intake stopped: the environment was invalid."

ASK "Does the bug prevent the user from completing the task? Type exactly: yes or no" AS blocked
IF @blocked is anything other than yes or no
    RETURN "Bug intake stopped: the blocked answer was invalid."

ASK "List the steps needed to reproduce the bug." AS steps
ASK "What should have happened?" AS expected
ASK "What actually happened?" AS actual

SET severity = "low"

IF @environment == "production"
    IF @blocked == "yes"
        SET severity = "critical"
    ELSE
        SET severity = "high"
ELSE
    IF @blocked == "yes"
        SET severity = "medium"

PRINT "All required information was collected. Generating the report now."

DO Create the Markdown bug report using @title, @severity, @environment,
    @steps, @expected, and @actual. Follow @report_format exactly and return
    only the completed report as a string. AS bug_report

PRINT @bug_report
RETURN "Bug intake completed."
